<title>USA: TABLE-Harte-Hanks Q2 oper shr $0.41 vs $0.33.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Harte-Hanks Q2 oper shr $0.41 vs $0.33.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.42		    $0.10</p>
<p> Net			 16,345		    3,906</p>
<p> Revs		     150,964		  122,285</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	38,832		   38,551</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	38,841		   38,702</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.68		    $0.32</p>
<p> Net			 26,362		   12,223</p>
<p> Revs		     289,388		  237,791</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	38,782		   38,420</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	38,824		   38,495</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: On an operating basis the company earned $0.41 per share in Q2 1997 and $0.33 per share in Q2 1996.</p>
<p>Revenues shown above exclude those from the company's television and newspaper operations, which Harte-Hanks agreed to sell on May 16.</p>
<p>Net earnings in 1996 include $12.1 million in expenses related to the pooling-of-interest acquisition of DiMark Inc in April 1996.</p>
